                    "font": "belerenb",
                    "size": 0.0324
                },
                "rules": {
                    "name": "Rules Text",
                    "text": "Target creature you control becomes a copy of target creature until end of turn.{flavor}I envy them, those who can’t see. Those who know not, that they are not. And those who live, blithe and free, sins forgotten and thus absolved. A fresh dawn in their playground, while we live in shadows, swimming in ink. We are but a fragile dream, a singular weed, resisting, ever resisting.\n- Masked Woman",
